			<heading>
				Eliphaz Speaks: Job’s Wickedness Is Great
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said:</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">Surely he who is wise is profitable to himself.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">make your ways blameless?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">enters into judgment with you?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">There is no end to your iniquities.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and stripped the naked of their clothing.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">withheld bread from the hungry.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">the favored man lived in it.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">and<crossref let="k" cid="c18022009.3" />the arms of the fatherless were crushed.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">and sudden terror overwhelms you,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">and a<crossref let="o" cid="c18022011.3" />flood of water covers you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">the highest stars, how lofty they are!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">the deep darkness?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">and he walks on the vault of heaven.’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">that wicked men have trod?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">their foundation was washed away.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">‘What can the Almighty do to us?’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">the counsel of the wicked is far from me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">mocks at them,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">the fire has consumed.’</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">thereby good will come to you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">lay up his words in your heart.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">remove injustice far from your tents,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">Ophir among the stones of the torrent-bed,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">and your precious silver.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">lift up your face to God.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">pay your vows.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">light will shine on your ways.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">the lowly.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">the cleanness of your hands.”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18022031">
			</marker>
			<end-paragraph>
			</end-paragraph>
